course: dictionary
lesson: 6051
title: Mentality: how a group thinks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mentality is the usual way a person or group thinks and feels about things. It is their attitude, the way they tend to see the world. Context helps: «a winning mentality» means a way of thinking that expects to win.
explain: The word can describe one person or a whole group. «A team mentality» describes a group that works together. Words like winning, growth and team are clues, so read the words around the word to see what kind of mentality is meant.
explain: Mentality can also be negative. In «mob mentality», people in a crowd do things they would never do alone. The example says this is sometimes called mob mentality, and «everyone did it» does not make it fine. Being part of a group does not make an action right.
fact: Mentality means the usual way a person or group thinks and feels about things.
fact: «A winning mentality» means a way of thinking that expects to win.
fact: «A growth mentality» means believing you can get better with effort.
fact: «Mob mentality» means people in a crowd acting in ways they would not act alone.
fact: In a formal sense, mentality can also mean a person's mind or thinking ability.
exercise: What does mentality mean? | A type of mountain | A loud noise in a crowd | * The usual way a person or group thinks and feels about things | A kind of sport
exercise: «A growth mentality» means believing you can do what? | Sleep for longer | Win every game without practising | * Get better with effort | Never try anything new
exercise: «In a group people often act worse than each would alone.» What is this sometimes called? | * Mob mentality | A team mentality | A winning mentality | A growth mentality
test: Mob mentality means people in a crowd do what? | Always work together kindly | * Do things they would not do alone | Stay silent and still | Only what they would do alone
test: Someone says, «Everyone did it, so it must be fine.» Using the example, what is the best reply? | Mentality means a mountain | Groups never do anything wrong | * Being in a group does not make an action right | Everyone doing it always makes it fine
exam: Jayden thinks mentality is a kind of hat. What is the correct meaning? | * A person's or group's usual way of thinking and feeling | A place where people meet | Fashion for hats | A quick cough
